"Usage: mqtt_client [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --uauthority <UAUTHORITY>\n          Authority for the local client identity [default: authority-a]\n      --uentity <UENTITY>\n          UEntity ID for local client identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x14321]\n      --uversion <UVERSION>\n          UEntity major version for local client identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x1]\n      --resource <RESOURCE>\n          Resource ID for local client identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x0]\n      --target-authority <TARGET_AUTHORITY>\n          Authority for the target service URI [default: authority-b]\n      --target-uentity <TARGET_UENTITY>\n          UEntity ID for target service URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x11236]\n      --target-uversion <TARGET_UVERSION>\n          UEntity major version for target service URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x1]\n      --target-resource <TARGET_RESOURCE>\n          Resource ID for target service URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x0421]\n      --broker-uri <BROKER_URI>\n          MQTT broker URI in host:port format [default: localhost:1883]\n      --send-count <SEND_COUNT>\n          Number of requests to send before exiting (0 means run forever) [default: 0]\n      --send-interval-ms <SEND_INTERVAL_MS>\n          Milliseconds to wait between request sends [default: 1000]\n      --timeout-ms <TIMEOUT_MS>\n          Milliseconds to wait for an observed response after bounded sends [default: 5000]\n      --encoding <ENCODING>\n          Payload encoding for the classic UMessage request payload [default: protobuf] [possible values: native, protobuf, xcdrv2, arrow, omgidl]\n      --payload <PAYLOAD>\n          Text payload used by non-Protobuf example messages [default: mqtt-client]\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n"
